Error [E0120]: this loop can't take handles out of a field or index
  --> tests/ui/loop_task_list_index.jet:4:19
    |
  4 |     loop h, groups[0] -> total += h.join() ?? 0
    |                   ^^^
 Why: each step hands you the handle itself, and a task handle cannot be copied — so the loop takes the whole list with the move marker `^`
 Fix: bind the list into a local this scope owns first (`hs := …`), then write `loop h, hs { … }`

Error [E0140]: `groups` still owes `consume`
  --> tests/ui/loop_task_list_index.jet:2:5
    |
  2 |     groups :: [[task 1, task 2]]
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: this value's type is `#SingleUse`, so it carries a job that has to be done — dropping it without doing that job leaves the work undone (an unjoined task, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: consume it exactly once: move it to a parameter with the move marker `^`, or `return` it — or write `#Unsafe("reason") { consume(groups) }` to discard it deliberately
